1
00:00:02,170 --> 00:00:03,920
Previously on The Big Bang Theory:

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:06,020
This is just a minor setback.

3
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:07,310
No, it's not, okay?

4
00:00:07,310 --> 00:00:08,910
I've been out here for, like, ten years.

5
00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:10,650
I have nothing to show for it.

6
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:12,570
Well, you have me.

7
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:17,100
I do have you.

8
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:24,260
Leonard Hofstadter,

9
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:26,250
will you marry me?

10
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:33,850
Did you seriously just say, "Um..."?

11
00:00:34,890 --> 00:00:37,430
- It's an outrage. - I know.

12
00:00:37,430 --> 00:00:39,770
The university-- they think they can do whatever they want.

13
00:00:39,770 --> 00:00:41,430
We just have to sit there and take it.

14
00:00:41,430 --> 00:00:42,630
You need to let it go, Sheldon.

15
00:00:42,630 --> 00:00:45,800
You work tirelessly for someone, and this is what you get.

16
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:46,450
Oh, my God!

17
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:49,800
They're just making you use your vacation days!

18
00:00:50,970 --> 00:00:52,610
But I don't want a vacation.

19
00:00:52,610 --> 00:00:55,320
Okay, listen, I don't mean to diminish what you're going through,

20
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:57,240
but I'm a little distracted right now.

21
00:00:57,240 --> 00:00:59,080
Oh, this again?

22
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:01,720
So, Penny proposed, you didn't say yes,

23
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,840
and now you think you may have lost her love forever.

24
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:05,810
How does this compare to me being forced

25
00:01:05,810 --> 00:01:08,490
to relax for a few days?

26
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:12,420
- It doesn't! - Thank you!

27
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:15,900
I'm gonna go talk to Penny.

28
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,070
I'm going to go inside, put on my coziest pajamas,

29
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:20,340
curl up with a good book

30
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:22,870
and wait for this nightmare to be over.

31
00:01:26,650 --> 00:01:27,700
Penny.

32
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:36,140
Sorry.

33
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:40,550
Hey. Look, I'm sorry I didn't text you back.

34
00:01:40,550 --> 00:01:41,980
I just needed some time to think.

35
00:01:41,980 --> 00:01:44,010
- Okay. - Here. Come in.

36
00:01:44,010 --> 00:01:46,040
Look, if you want to break up, just say it.

37
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:47,520
- Leonard... - No, no, no, no. I take it back.

38
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:49,740
Don't say it. Just-just hate me, but stay with me.

39
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:51,830
It worked for my parents.

40
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:56,460
Listen, I don't want to break up with you.

41
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:59,040
Oh. O-Okay.

42
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:00,980
Good, good.

43
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:03,640
So, it's cool if I cry a little?

44
00:02:04,590 --> 00:02:06,700
Yeah, I probably wouldn't.

45
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:08,750
Yeah.

46
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:11,800
Look, you did the right thing last night.

47
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:13,130
I was a mess.

48
00:02:13,130 --> 00:02:15,580
I was just frustrated because my career is going nowhere.

49
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:17,570
Look, I get it, and I want you to know

50
00:02:17,610 --> 00:02:20,120
that I support whatever you want to do.

51
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:22,010
Great, because I've been thinking,

52
00:02:22,010 --> 00:02:23,560
if I really want this acting thing to work,

53
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,680
I need to focus all my energy on it.

54
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:26,770
And to do that,

55
00:02:26,770 --> 00:02:30,230
I should quit waitressing at The Cheesecake Factory.

56
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:33,640
- That-That's a big step. - I know.

57
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:35,750
So, you know, before making any rash...

58
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:38,720
- I already quit. - And I support you!

59
00:03:05,390 --> 00:03:07,820
- Come on, take me to work with you. - No.

60
00:03:07,820 --> 00:03:09,980
- You're on vacation. - Please.

61
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:11,620
What if there's a big breakthrough in science today

62
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:13,020
and I'm not there to see it?

63
00:03:13,020 --> 00:03:14,530
Do you really think there's gonna be a breakthrough

64
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:15,740
without you there to do it?

65
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:18,190
No. I was just tricking you.

66
00:03:19,110 --> 00:03:20,740
Bye.

67
00:03:22,590 --> 00:03:24,160
Leonard, wait!

68
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:25,960
- Take me with you.- No!

69
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:28,170
- Please. - No!

70
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:29,520
Too bad. I'm coming with you.

71
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:31,030
- Oh, Sheldon, stay! - But...

72
00:03:31,030 --> 00:03:33,800
I said stay!

73
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:42,010
I'm going to work.

74
00:03:42,010 --> 00:03:45,100
Do not follow me.

75
00:04:02,620 --> 00:04:03,900
Hey, Stuart.

76
00:04:06,010 --> 00:04:07,430
- Hey. - Sorry. Did I startle you?

77
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:10,480
Yes, but at this point, pretty much any customer does.

78
00:04:11,890 --> 00:04:12,910
What can I do for you?

79
00:04:12,910 --> 00:04:14,400
Well, I need a little help.

80
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:17,160
I accidentally destroyed one of Howard's comic books this morning,

81
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:18,930
and I was hoping I could replace it.

82
00:04:18,930 --> 00:04:20,360
Wow. What happened?

83
00:04:20,370 --> 00:04:23,580
Batman got his ass kicked by my curling iron.

84
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:27,590
Well, don't let The Riddler know that.

85
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:31,400
It's a comic book joke.

86
00:04:32,330 --> 00:04:34,460
Or maybe it's not.

87
00:04:35,270 --> 00:04:36,390
Do you have this one?

88
00:04:36,390 --> 00:04:38,210
Uh, well, it's-it's pretty rare.

89
00:04:38,210 --> 00:04:40,640
Can you give me a few days to track it down?

90
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:41,860
Ooh, I was kind of hoping to get it

91
00:04:41,860 --> 00:04:43,450
before Howie comes home from work.

92
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:44,520
Oh. What's the hurry?

93
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:45,510
Well, he's always saying

94
00:04:45,510 --> 00:04:47,700
I should be more careful with my curling iron,

95
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:49,040
and it seems like a dangerous precedent

96
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:51,230
to let him think he can be right.

97
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:54,040
Well, I'll do what I can,

98
00:04:54,070 --> 00:04:56,610
but I can't make any promises.

99
00:04:56,610 --> 00:05:00,560
You know, I do work at a pharmaceutical company.

100
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:02,300
If you can make this happen today,

101
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:04,800
I can hook you up with anxiety medication,

102
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:07,610
- antidepressants. - Really?

103
00:05:08,810 --> 00:05:11,090
Do you have any of these?

104
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:18,530
Hello, Mr. Rat Brain.

105
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:21,140
Not so bitey without the rest of the rat

106
00:05:21,170 --> 00:05:23,120
to back us up now, are we?

107
00:05:24,070 --> 00:05:25,370
Anybody home?

108
00:05:25,370 --> 00:05:26,400
Hey, what brings you guys here?

109
00:05:26,410 --> 00:05:27,640
Well, we were just on our way to lunch

110
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,890
and wanted to see if you'd like to join.

111
00:05:29,890 --> 00:05:30,690
Why?

112
00:05:30,690 --> 00:05:31,950
Because Sheldon's not here this week,

113
00:05:31,950 --> 00:05:33,430
and you don't think I have any other options?

114
00:05:33,430 --> 00:05:35,480
I'm just kidding. I'll get my purse.

115
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:37,490
Hi, Amy. I... Oh.

116
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:40,480
I'm sorry. I didn't know you had any company.

117
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,310
That's okay.

118
00:05:41,310 --> 00:05:42,960
Uh, Bert, this is Howard and Rajesh.

119
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:44,410
Guys, this is Bert.

120
00:05:44,410 --> 00:05:45,560
- Hey. Good to see you. - Hey.

121
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:46,870
Anyway, I wanted to show you

122
00:05:46,870 --> 00:05:49,840
this tourmalinated quartz that we got in the lab.

123
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:51,200
This is so pretty.

124
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,830
- Bert works for the geology department. - Yeah.

125
00:05:53,830 --> 00:05:57,000
You know what, uh, geologists and Bon Jovi have in common?

126
00:05:57,460 --> 00:05:59,480
You're both into rock?

127
00:06:01,590 --> 00:06:03,290
Yeah.

128
00:06:05,250 --> 00:06:06,720
Well, see ya.

129
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:08,870
Oh, you forgot your quartz.

130
00:06:08,870 --> 00:06:10,510
Oh, it's okay.

131
00:06:10,510 --> 00:06:12,510
I want you to have it.

132
00:06:12,510 --> 00:06:14,430
Bye.

133
00:06:14,430 --> 00:06:16,320
He's nice.

134
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:19,220
Yeah, he's nice because he likes you.

135
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:21,760
What?! No, he doesn't.

136
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:23,490
He brought you a pretty rock.

137
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:25,200
So? He does that every day...Oh.

138
00:06:28,060 --> 00:06:29,220
You know, if you'd rather skip lunch

139
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:31,970
and hang out with your boyfriend Bert, it's totally okay.

140
00:06:31,970 --> 00:06:33,340
He's not my boyfriend.

141
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:35,310
Are you sure? He's tall, pale and awkward.

142
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:37,390
That sounds like your type.

143
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:40,960
Should someone as lonely as you really be making fun of me?

144
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:43,390
Yeah, grow up, Howard. God.

145
00:06:44,790 --> 00:06:47,460
What do I do? I don't want to hurt his feelings.

146
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:49,860
Maybe the problem is he thinks you're available.

147
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:51,560
Does he know you're dating Sheldon?

148
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:53,890
I guess it hasn't come up.

149
00:06:53,890 --> 00:06:55,560
There you go.

150
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:58,430
And does Sheldon know you're dating Sheldon?

151
00:07:00,830 --> 00:07:03,470
I'm sorry. Who are you dating?

152
00:07:03,470 --> 00:07:05,790
Yeah, knock it off, Howard!

153
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:16,690
Hey, Sheldon.

154
00:07:16,690 --> 00:07:18,570
Hello.

155
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:26,700
You okay?

156
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:30,120
I'm on vacation. What do you think?

157
00:07:31,050 --> 00:07:33,130
Why are you sitting in the stairwell?

158
00:07:33,780 --> 00:07:36,320
Leonard told me to stay.

159
00:07:37,170 --> 00:07:40,410
Oh. Well, good boy.

160
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:42,830
Where are you going?

161
00:07:42,830 --> 00:07:43,970
Oh, I have a ton of errands to run.

162
00:07:43,970 --> 00:07:45,140
I need to make copies of my headshot,

163
00:07:45,140 --> 00:07:46,220
send them off to agents

164
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:48,640
and sign up for a new acting class and...

165
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:51,170
- Well, have fun. - Okay.

166
00:07:57,620 --> 00:08:00,280
- You want to come with me? - Really?

167
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:03,390
Come on, boy. Come on. Let's go. Let's go.

168
00:08:03,390 --> 00:08:06,260
Get in the car. Come on.

169
00:08:07,990 --> 00:08:09,600
All right, thanks a lot.

170
00:08:10,550 --> 00:08:12,270
They have one at Capital Comics.

171
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:14,270
- Oh, that's great. - No, it's not.

172
00:08:14,270 --> 00:08:15,840
I hate that place.

173
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:17,910
Guy who owns it is a jerk.

174
00:08:17,910 --> 00:08:20,210
He's always making me feel bad about myself.

175
00:08:20,210 --> 00:08:21,910
Oh, that's terrible.

176
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:24,660
What's the address?

177
00:08:25,850 --> 00:08:27,110
You know, why don't I just take you there?

178
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,890
That way, I can make sure he doesn't rip you off.

179
00:08:28,890 --> 00:08:30,810
Oh, thanks, but I don't want you to close up.

180
00:08:30,810 --> 00:08:33,000
I mean, won't you lose business?

181
00:08:35,590 --> 00:08:37,770
Sorry. That was mean.

182
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:43,800
- Penny really quit The Cheesecake Factory? - Yeah.

183
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:46,140
- So, what is she doing today? - I don't know.

184
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:47,600
She already thinks I don't support this,

185
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:50,080
so if I call, it might look like I'm checking up on her.

186
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:51,260
Well, do you support this?

187
00:08:51,260 --> 00:08:52,530
Of course I do.

188
00:08:52,530 --> 00:08:53,870
She's a great actress.

189
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:55,780
I'm proud she's taking this risk.

190
00:08:55,780 --> 00:08:56,710
That's nice.

191
00:08:56,710 --> 00:08:59,200
You bought that? Great!

192
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:04,600
I got to call her before I forget how I said it.

193
00:09:07,150 --> 00:09:08,320
Hi. What's up?

194
00:09:08,330 --> 00:09:09,090
Oh, how's it going?

195
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:10,530
You taking Hollywood by storm?

196
00:09:10,530 --> 00:09:12,170
Actually, I'm at The Cheesecake Factory.

197
00:09:12,170 --> 00:09:14,590
You got your job back. That is great news.

198
00:09:14,590 --> 00:09:16,100
I didn't want to say anything,

199
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:17,720
but you are making the right choice.

200
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,050
To plunge yourself into debt right now

201
00:09:19,050 --> 00:09:21,300
- would be literally insane. Yeah.

202
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:23,860
I'm just returning my uniform.

203
00:09:26,290 --> 00:09:29,220
And I support you.

204
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:36,940
Before we begin your guided meditation,

205
00:09:36,940 --> 00:09:37,800
close your eyes

206
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:41,300
and picture yourself in a peaceful environment.

207
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:43,320
Okay.

208
00:09:44,390 --> 00:09:49,090
I'm inside the CERN super collider.

209
00:09:49,690 --> 00:09:53,330
Now, take a deep, relaxing breath in through your nose.

210
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,890
And let it out.

211
00:09:56,890 --> 00:09:59,690
Didn't see that coming.

212
00:10:00,950 --> 00:10:02,290
In.

213
00:10:04,070 --> 00:10:05,400
Let me guess.

214
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:07,160
And out.

215
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:12,190
What was I gonna do? Two "ins" in a row?

216
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:16,720
Where's my lemonade?

217
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:18,390
I didn't get it.

218
00:10:18,910 --> 00:10:21,490
A fitting swan song to your career as a waitress

219
00:10:21,490 --> 00:10:24,440
to forget my order one last time.

220
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:32,880
Do you think quitting my job was a mistake?

221
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:36,470
Do you see me drinking lemonade?

222
00:10:37,140 --> 00:10:38,920
No. I'm serious.

223
00:10:39,580 --> 00:10:40,940
Why do you ask?

224
00:10:41,010 --> 00:10:43,210
Because Leonard just pissed me off.

225
00:10:43,210 --> 00:10:45,380
Am I being an idiot or not?

226
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:47,850
No, I don't think you are.

227
00:10:47,850 --> 00:10:49,210
Really?

228
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:52,150
The best way to achieve a goal is to devote 100%

229
00:10:52,150 --> 00:10:54,510
of your time and energy to it.

230
00:10:54,510 --> 00:10:56,650
When I decided I was going to be a physicist,

231
00:10:56,650 --> 00:10:58,190
I didn't take some other job

232
00:10:58,190 --> 00:11:00,110
in case it didn't work out.

233
00:11:00,110 --> 00:11:02,130
Which wasn't easy because there was a lot of pressure

234
00:11:02,130 --> 00:11:05,500
from Ms. Pierson for me to be chalk monitor that year.

235
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,270
Thank you. I needed to hear that.

236
00:11:09,270 --> 00:11:11,700
Why can't Leonard understand it?

237
00:11:12,370 --> 00:11:14,680
Because he's not like us, Penny.

238
00:11:15,590 --> 00:11:17,530
We're dreamers.

239
00:11:19,510 --> 00:11:20,870
Yeah, I need to start cracking the window

240
00:11:20,870 --> 00:11:23,000
when I leave you in the car.

241
00:11:31,290 --> 00:11:32,520
Hello, Bert.

242
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:36,080
So, anyway, there's this big, uh, rock and mineral show

243
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:37,350
next week in Santa Monica and...

244
00:11:37,350 --> 00:11:39,030
Listen, um, Bert,

245
00:11:39,030 --> 00:11:41,820
before you say anything else, I...

246
00:11:41,820 --> 00:11:44,000
I have a boyfriend.

247
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,540
This is awkward.

248
00:11:46,540 --> 00:11:48,290
You thought I was gonna ask you to go with me

249
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:51,940
to the mineral show. - Weren't you?

250
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:53,940
Yeah.

251
00:11:56,250 --> 00:11:57,970
That's very nice of you, but...

252
00:11:57,970 --> 00:12:00,000
I do have a boyfriend.

253
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,660
That's what you all say.

254
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:02,860
You just don't want to go out with me

255
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:05,020
because I have an off-putting personality.

256
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:06,700
No, that's not true.

257
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:09,230
My boyfriend has an off-putting personality, too.

258
00:12:09,230 --> 00:12:11,420
Like, way worse than you.

259
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:14,460
Don't worry.

260
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:15,590
I'm used to it.

261
00:12:15,590 --> 00:12:19,270
I mean, I'm big and weird and funny-looking

262
00:12:19,270 --> 00:12:21,910
and no one ever wants to do anything with me.

263
00:12:21,910 --> 00:12:24,330
Don't say that.

264
00:12:24,330 --> 00:12:25,870
It's okay.

265
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:27,650
I know I'm a monster.

266
00:12:27,650 --> 00:12:30,010
No, Bert, come on.

267
00:12:30,540 --> 00:12:33,120
I'd love to go to the mineral show with you.

268
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,110
Sweet.

269
00:12:34,110 --> 00:12:36,000
It's a date.

270
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:39,790
No, it's not.

271
00:12:39,790 --> 00:12:41,440
Too late!

272
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:55,240
Yeah. Haven't seen this many people in my store

273
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:56,800
since that Korean church bus

274
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:58,970
crashed through my front window.

275
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:01,650
Hey! Stuart!

276
00:13:01,650 --> 00:13:02,590
Jesse.

277
00:13:02,590 --> 00:13:04,430
Haven't seen you in forever.

278
00:13:04,430 --> 00:13:06,080
Look how gray you've gotten.

279
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:08,390
My hair's exactly the same color as always.

280
00:13:08,390 --> 00:13:10,950
No, I was talking about your skin.

281
00:13:11,850 --> 00:13:14,270
Look, uh, my friend here needs a comic book...

282
00:13:14,270 --> 00:13:16,900
And she went into your store by mistake.

283
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:19,450
Good thing there was no one there to see you.

284
00:13:19,970 --> 00:13:21,330
What do you need?

285
00:13:22,130 --> 00:13:23,470
Oh, yeah, yeah. I got this.

286
00:13:23,470 --> 00:13:25,290
Right over here.

287
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:29,320
Even you, Sweatpants?

288
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:31,600
Free popcorn.

289
00:13:32,950 --> 00:13:34,440
Can I offer you a coffee?

290
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:35,930
Espresso? Latte?

291
00:13:35,930 --> 00:13:36,650
No, thanks.

292
00:13:36,650 --> 00:13:38,830
How about you, Stu? Mocha? Scone?

293
00:13:38,830 --> 00:13:42,330
Directions to the nearest soup kitchen?

294
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:46,670
He knows where the soup kitchen is.

295
00:13:48,610 --> 00:13:50,650
It's on Merton Avenue.

296
00:13:52,130 --> 00:13:54,390
I don't think I like the way you're treating my friend.

297
00:13:54,390 --> 00:13:55,810
Sorry.

298
00:13:55,810 --> 00:13:57,330
You want the book or not?

299
00:13:57,330 --> 00:13:58,660
Not from you.

300
00:13:58,660 --> 00:14:00,730
Let's go, Stuart.

301
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:05,550
You know something, Jesse?

302
00:14:05,550 --> 00:14:07,810
You may have a successful business

303
00:14:07,810 --> 00:14:09,670
a-and the kind of pink complexion

304
00:14:09,670 --> 00:14:11,860
that comes with good nutrition...

305
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:14,880
...but I have something more important.

306
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:16,450
What's that?

307
00:14:16,450 --> 00:14:19,490
Friendship.

308
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:24,360
Which I would trade in a heartbeat for all of this.

309
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,770
The mineral and rock show?

310
00:14:29,770 --> 00:14:33,090
That would be awful even without Bert.

311
00:14:33,670 --> 00:14:35,700
So what am I supposed to do now?

312
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:39,280
Prepare your uterus for his gigantic offspring?

313
00:14:41,350 --> 00:14:43,090
This isn't funny.

314
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:44,410
I'm gonna have to tell him the truth:

315
00:14:44,410 --> 00:14:45,950
that even if I didn't have a boyfriend,

316
00:14:45,950 --> 00:14:47,530
I wouldn't be interested in him.

317
00:14:47,530 --> 00:14:49,700
I've heard those words so many times.

318
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:51,890
From Linda Nosenchuck, Tammy Rosenworcel...

319
00:14:51,890 --> 00:14:53,710
Padma Kapur, Neha Chowdury...

320
00:14:53,710 --> 00:14:55,450
...Marci Grossman, Lisa Mazzarino...

321
00:14:55,450 --> 00:14:57,300
- ...Megan Pincus... - ...Tammy Cho...

322
00:14:57,300 --> 00:14:58,620
Oh, who was that girl from our Starbucks?

323
00:14:58,620 --> 00:15:01,600
- Arlene Russel! - Yes! Arlene!

324
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:06,840
She wrote "no way" on both our cappuccinos.

325
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:08,050
Poor Bert.

326
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:10,680
That guy's got a rough afternoon ahead of him.

327
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:12,570
Well, how would you want a girl

328
00:15:12,570 --> 00:15:14,570
to tell you she wasn't interested?

329
00:15:14,570 --> 00:15:17,510
I guess, uh, I'd like her to sit me down,

330
00:15:17,510 --> 00:15:19,640
look me in the eye and say,

331
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:22,380
"I was wrong. I love you."

332
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:26,040
And then maybe she could touch me in a special way.

333
00:15:27,100 --> 00:15:29,750
That's how you reject a guy.

334
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:31,240
Okay, I don't have time for this.

335
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:33,790
I'm just gonna go find him and be brutally honest.

336
00:15:33,790 --> 00:15:35,450
- No, don't. - He'll be so upset.

337
00:15:35,450 --> 00:15:36,950
He'll probably climb up the Empire State Building

338
00:15:36,950 --> 00:15:40,020
and start swatting at planes.

339
00:15:44,370 --> 00:15:46,000
You want us to talk to him?

340
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:47,040
Really?

341
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:48,620
- You would do that? - Sure.

342
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:49,760
We've both been in his shoes.

343
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:52,730
We'll let him down with compassion and respect.

344
00:15:52,730 --> 00:15:54,390
Thank you.

345
00:15:54,390 --> 00:15:56,430
Let's go.

346
00:15:57,730 --> 00:15:59,370
So we tell him she's a lesbian, right?

347
00:15:59,370 --> 00:16:01,790
Of course we tell him she's a lesbian.

348
00:16:09,590 --> 00:16:11,840
And hold three...

349
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:14,680
two... one.

350
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:16,620
Very good.

351
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:20,170
Now let's try Warrior II.

352
00:16:20,920 --> 00:16:23,180
And hold.

353
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:27,710
I've read that there are great yogis

354
00:16:27,710 --> 00:16:30,080
who have such mastery over their bodies

355
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:33,890
they can draw water in through their genitals.

356
00:16:41,730 --> 00:16:44,770
Yeah, well, I don't think we're gonna get to do that today.

357
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:48,070
Too bad.

358
00:16:48,070 --> 00:16:49,730
It seems like a good way to drink a milk shake

359
00:16:49,730 --> 00:16:52,290
without getting brain freeze.

360
00:16:55,910 --> 00:16:59,180
And now we go to Reverse Warrior.

361
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:05,660
How did she get you to do yoga?

362
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:09,920
Well, to be honest, I thought she said "Yoda."

363
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:15,230
I'm helping him relax because, unlike you,

364
00:17:15,230 --> 00:17:16,730
he supports me.

365
00:17:16,730 --> 00:17:18,740
Oh, how many times do I have to say it?

366
00:17:18,740 --> 00:17:20,370
I support you.

367
00:17:20,370 --> 00:17:21,880
Sheldon, take a break.

368
00:17:22,860 --> 00:17:24,790
Namaste.

369
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:28,900
Okay, if you support me, what was with that phone call?

370
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:31,460
Fine. I'm not sure you should have quit.

371
00:17:31,460 --> 00:17:32,910
But if you care so much what I think,

372
00:17:32,910 --> 00:17:34,610
why didn't you ask me before you did it?

373
00:17:34,610 --> 00:17:36,200
Oh, so now I need your permission?

374
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:38,720
Would you have asked me before you quit your job?

375
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,690
Yes.

376
00:17:39,690 --> 00:17:41,220
I thought we were in the kind of relationship

377
00:17:41,220 --> 00:17:42,570
where we make decisions together.

378
00:17:42,570 --> 00:17:44,190
If I'm wrong, then maybe we need to talk about

379
00:17:44,190 --> 00:17:46,010
the kind of relationship we're actually in.

380
00:17:46,010 --> 00:17:47,440
Yeah, well, maybe we do.

381
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:49,820
I'm willing to if you guys are.

382
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:52,970
Can we please have some privacy?

383
00:17:52,970 --> 00:17:54,230
Y... No.

384
00:17:54,230 --> 00:17:56,430
I'm as much a part of this relationship as you two,

385
00:17:56,430 --> 00:17:59,160
and I think it's high time we put all our cards on the table.

386
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:01,620
Yeah. For example, where is this going?

387
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:03,610
Are you two ever getting married?

388
00:18:03,610 --> 00:18:05,690
And, if so, where will we all live?

389
00:18:05,690 --> 00:18:07,990
Have you thought about that?

390
00:18:07,990 --> 00:18:09,880
- No. - Penny?

391
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:11,370
Okay, wait. What are we doing?

392
00:18:11,370 --> 00:18:13,420
For some reason, we're planning a future

393
00:18:13,420 --> 00:18:15,510
where we both live with Sheldon forever.

394
00:18:15,510 --> 00:18:18,660
Good. Now we're getting somewhere.

395
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:20,780
Look, I know you think I'm being reckless,

396
00:18:20,780 --> 00:18:21,670
and you might be right,

397
00:18:21,670 --> 00:18:23,140
but I need to take this shot.

398
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:24,230
Yeah, no kidding.

399
00:18:24,230 --> 00:18:26,000
Despite what it says on her resume,

400
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,500
she is no longer 22.

401
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:34,130
I swear, I am on your side.

402
00:18:34,130 --> 00:18:35,680
You keep saying you're on my side,

403
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,970
- but you don't act like it. - He does that to me, too.

404
00:18:37,970 --> 00:18:40,560
Why do we put up with it?

405
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:44,580
Listen, I could never do what you're doing, okay?

406
00:18:44,580 --> 00:18:46,270
I would be terrified.

407
00:18:46,270 --> 00:18:47,690
Well, it's scary for me, too.

408
00:18:47,690 --> 00:18:49,630
I'm fine with it.

409
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:53,780
My point is, just because I couldn't do it

410
00:18:53,780 --> 00:18:55,150
doesn't mean you shouldn't.

411
00:18:55,150 --> 00:18:58,180
And I'm proud of you.

412
00:18:59,690 --> 00:19:02,740
Okay. Thank you.

413
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:04,610
Well, to celebrate this reconciliation,

414
00:19:04,610 --> 00:19:06,400
let's all share a milk shake.

415
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:09,220
Uh, Penny, you'll need a straw.

416
00:19:15,260 --> 00:19:16,700
- You're back. - Yes, I am!

417
00:19:16,700 --> 00:19:18,360
There's a few more things I want to say to you.

418
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:20,040
Stuart's store is just fine,

419
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:21,670
and he's a much nicer person than you are,

420
00:19:21,670 --> 00:19:22,810
and if you still have that comic,

421
00:19:22,810 --> 00:19:25,530
I'd like to buy it right now!

422
00:19:25,910 --> 00:19:27,450
No problem.

423
00:19:27,450 --> 00:19:29,660
Oh, you want a latte while you wait?

424
00:19:29,660 --> 00:19:31,640
No, I don't want a latte!

425
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:34,830
I want a cappuccino and a blueberry scone!

426
00:19:34,830 --> 00:19:36,680
I only have chocolate chip.

427
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:39,870
Well, that sounds even better!

428
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:49,340
Thanks for coming to the mineral and rock show with me.

429
00:19:52,830 --> 00:19:55,470
We're sorry Amy didn't want to go.

430
00:19:55,470 --> 00:19:59,050
Really, really sorry.

431
00:19:59,790 --> 00:20:02,400
Who needs her when I have you guys?

432
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:04,300
Rock show!

433
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:06,010
Rock show! Rock show!

434
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:08,070
Rock show! Rock show!

435
00:20:08,070 --> 00:20:09,980
Rock show!

436
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:14,250
Rock show...!

